            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-AKb7dZd28oGdcHxKd4nlXjIlgdh\">Regarding food purchases from supermarkets, Country B led in 1998 with approximately 22% of food being bought from these establishments, which was about twice the figure for Country A and four times that of Country C, at around 10% and 5% respectively. By 2008, however, Country A had overtaken Country B, with its percentage rising dramatically to 35%, while Country B saw a modest increase to 27%. Meanwhile, Country C's figure doubled to approximately 10% by the end of the period.</div>\n</div>",
