            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-LQOedsgyAowxrjxvIY4lTaiqgvh\">As for goods bought from supermarkets, the pattern was somewhat similar. Country B again recorded the highest percentage in 1998, at roughly 23%, while Country A's figure stood at just 5%, and no data was available for Country C. Over the following decade, Country A witnessed a substantial surge to about 40%, surpassing Country B's figure of 25%. Country C reported approximately 15% of goods being purchased from supermarkets in 2008.</div>\n</div>",
